  notes: "Operator 2026-10-14: the real cell uses the right base from the hand-eye calibration, NOT the tape-measured/Isaac layout (y -0.4474, rpy 0; old file kept as dual_arm_calibration.nominal_20261006.yaml.bak). arm_right_base: scan_results/dual_arm_calibration_20261012/calib2.yaml (camera-only joint solve, 70 left + 60 right board samples, table images excluded; std xyz mm [0.25, 0.23, 0.2], rpy deg [0.019, 0.023, 0.022]; identical to composing ~/.ros2/easy_handeye2/calibrations/dualcal_20261009_left_single.calib with the inverse of dualcal_20261009_right_single.calib) = xyz mm (-1.3, -454.3, +4.8), rpy deg (-1.04, +0.48, +2.81). camera_link: dualcal_20261012_left_hovercorr.calib (calib2 camera + hover correction (-5.9, +6.3, 0) mm), the calibration the left-arm cutting stack uses. TRUST GATE FAIL (no touch check points yet): recommended padding 20 mm; verify with right-arm touches/check stickers (plan P2) before relying on it near the other arm."
